      {
        "id": "def-spherical-bessel-and-hankel-functions",
        "kind": "definition",
        "title": "Spherical Bessel and outgoing Hankel function conventions",
        "deps": [
          "def-sine-and-cosine-by-power-series",
          "def-complex-exponential"
        ],
        "justified_by": [
          "lem-spherical-bessel-and-hankel-radial-solutions"
        ],
        "dependency_level": 0,
        "source_path": "items/def-spherical-bessel-and-hankel-functions.md",
        "statement": "For real $z>0$, let $D_z:=z^{-1}\\frac{d}{dz}$ and define, for integers $\\ell\\ge0$,\n$$j_\\ell(z):=(-z)^\\ell D_z^\\ell\\left(\\frac{\\sin z}{z}\\right),\\qquad h_\\ell^{(1)}(z):=(-z)^\\ell D_z^\\ell\\left(-i\\frac{e^{iz}}{z}\\right).$$\nThe definition fixes the outgoing $e^{iz}$ convention. The functions solve the radial Helmholtz equation and have the recurrence, origin, Wronskian, and infinity behavior by [[lem-spherical-bessel-and-hankel-radial-solutions]].\n\nThese symbolic definitions assert no stable or certified numerical evaluation algorithm for large $\\ell$ or $z$.",
        "strategy": "not-applicable",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "literature-derived",
          "proof": "not-applicable"
        },
        "axiom_use": "No axiom is used. These are exact symbolic functions; no stable or certified evaluation algorithm is asserted.",
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "Maximilian Kreuzer, Quantum Theory: Lecture Notes, Chapter 8",
              "url": "https://hep.itp.tuwien.ac.at/~kreuzer/Quanten.15.07.09.pdf",
              "locator": "PDF pp. 147–149, spherical Bessel equation, regular and outgoing radial solutions, and recurrences."
            },
            {
              "title": "Pierre Capel, Introduction to Scattering Theory, TALENT lecture notes",
              "url": "https://indico.mitp.uni-mainz.de/event/279/sessions/1001/attachments/2951/3418/Capel1TALENTFB22ho.pdf",
              "locator": "PDF pp. 18–19, spherical Bessel functions and recurrence relations; the local convention uses the outgoing Hankel sign fixed below."
            }
          ]
        },
        "status": "draft"
      },
      {
        "id": "lem-spherical-bessel-and-hankel-radial-solutions",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "title": "Spherical Bessel and outgoing Hankel recurrences solve the radial Helmholtz equation",
        "deps": [
          "def-spherical-bessel-and-hankel-functions",
          "thm-algebra-of-derivatives",
          "thm-chain-rule",
          "thm-sine-and-cosine-derivatives",
          "thm-eulers-formula",
          "thm-termwise-differentiation-of-a-real-power-series",
          "thm-power-series-uniform-on-compact-subintervals",
          "thm-ratio-test",
          "lem-sine-and-cosine-series-converge-everywhere",
          "def-factorial-and-falling-factorial",
          "lem-of-naturals-positive",
          "cor-zero-derivative-implies-constant",
          "lem-trigonometric-identities-machin-and-range-reduction"
        ],
        "justified_by": [],
        "dependency_level": 1,
        "source_path": "items/lem-spherical-bessel-and-hankel-radial-solutions.md",
        "statement": "For the functions of [[def-spherical-bessel-and-hankel-functions]], define\n$$L_\\ell y:=y''+\\frac2z y'+\\left(1-\\frac{\\ell(\\ell+1)}{z^2}\\right)y\\qquad(z>0).$$\nThen $L_\\ell j_\\ell=L_\\ell h_\\ell^{(1)}=0$, and for $y=j,h^{(1)}$,\n$$y_{\\ell+1}(z)=\\frac{\\ell}{z}y_\\ell(z)-y_\\ell'(z),\\qquad y_\\ell'(z)=y_{\\ell-1}(z)-\\frac{\\ell+1}{z}y_\\ell(z)\\quad(\\ell\\ge1).$$\nThe regular-origin and outgoing-infinity normalizations are\n$$j_\\ell(z)=\\frac{z^\\ell}{(2\\ell+1)!!}+O(z^{\\ell+2}),\\quad h_\\ell^{(1)}(z)=-i(2\\ell-1)!!z^{-\\ell-1}(1+O(z))\\quad(z\\downarrow0),$$\n$$j_\\ell(z)=\\frac{\\sin(z-\\ell\\pi/2)}z+O(z^{-2}),\\quad h_\\ell^{(1)}(z)=(-i)^{\\ell+1}\\frac{e^{iz}}z+O(z^{-2})\\quad(z\\to\\infty),$$\nwhere $(-1)!!:=1$. Their Wronskian is\n$$j_\\ell(z)(h_\\ell^{(1)})'(z)-j_\\ell'(z)h_\\ell^{(1)}(z)=\\frac{i}{z^2}.$$",
        "strategy": "direct",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "ai-altered",
          "proof": "ai-generated"
        },
        "axiom_use": "The proof uses finite differentiation and power-series algebra only; it makes no certified numerical evaluation claim.",
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "Maximilian Kreuzer, Quantum Theory: Lecture Notes, version July 15, 2009, Chapter 8",
              "url": "https://hep.itp.tuwien.ac.at/~kreuzer/Quanten.15.07.09.pdf",
              "locator": "PDF pp. 147–149, radial Helmholtz equation and spherical Bessel functions; the exact finite-derivative identities below are verified locally."
            },
            {
              "title": "Pierre Capel, Introduction to Scattering Theory, TALENT lecture notes",
              "url": "https://indico.mitp.uni-mainz.de/event/279/sessions/1001/attachments/2951/3418/Capel1TALENTFB22ho.pdf",
              "locator": "PDF pp. 18–19, spherical Bessel equation and recurrences."
            }
          ]
        },
