        ],
        "dependency_level": 3,
        "statement": "Every `success` output of [[alg-certified-scaled-spherical-bessel-evaluation]] encloses each requested scaled or unscaled value, or the entire requested image for an interval input, and satisfies its absolute-radius test. Its relative flags satisfy [[def-certified-evaluation-result-contract]]. Every capped execution terminates. For each fixed order, positive represented real point, finite nonempty target list, and positive rational absolute tolerances, some finite work, degree, interface-index, and precision caps permit absolute success. The same holds for an exact positive dyadic point. For a nonzero requested target, any positive rational relative tolerance can also eventually be certified by rerunning with sufficiently small positive rational absolute tolerances and sufficiently large finite caps; no relative certification is promised at a zero. The theorem gives no uniform floating-point condition number, bit-complexity bound, success guarantee for fixed small caps, or scattering uniqueness result."
